 "realtime_factor": 0.017026561567989873,
 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Roughly twice a week, carry a bag that's too big for shop and split each shop shop into two or fewer items. Each item should fit where your ticket is. A basket is great if you shop at a co op that has a good bag limit policy. Hang it where your ticket is, and carry only one item in each hand. Then a big bag that fits where your ticket is is worth it. If you also buy a loaf at the shop, the basket becomes a carryout bucket. A backpack is great for trips that one leg of which is by bike, but it's often too big for shop shopping. A bag that's too big is much slower.",
